 ## Operating characteristics
-
-*   **Time Complexity:** The dominant cost is the eigen-decomposition of the tensor for each voxel. The sources specify using the non-iterative approach by Hasan et al. [HBPA01], which is $O(1)$ per voxel but involves a fixed number of arithmetic operations. The directional filtering step is also $O(1)$ per voxel. Thus, the overhead is constant per sample point along the ray.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the tensor field. If eigenvectors are precomputed, an additional 3 floats per voxel are needed. If computed on the fly, no extra storage is required beyond the tensor data.
+*   **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
